<section class="nit nit-guarantee nit-section" aria-labelledby="nit-guarantee-heading">
  <div class="nit-container nit-guarantee__inner">
    <div class="nit-guarantee__head"><p class="nit-label nit-reveal">Guarantee</p><h2 class="nit-h1 nit-guarantee__heading nit-reveal" id="nit-guarantee-heading">
        If it fails, this is what happens
      </h2><div class="nit-body nit-measure nit-guarantee__lead nit-reveal">
          <p>A vacuum with a motor and a battery is a thing that can go wrong, and saying otherwise would be the least reassuring thing on this page. So here is the procedure, in the order it happens, including the parts of it that cost you nothing and the parts we do not cover.</p>
        </div></div>

    <div class="nit-guarantee__grid"><div class="nit-guarantee__figure nit-reveal"><div class="nit-media" style="--nit-ratio: 4/3"><img class="nit-media__img" src="{{ 'nitidus-guarantee.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Line drawing of the vacuum, annotated with which parts the two-year warranty covers: the motor and battery failure are covered; the filter is a consumable and accidental damage to the housing is not." width="1400" height="1050" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
</div>

      <div class="nit-guarantee__body"><div class="nit-guarantee__steps-wrap nit-reveal"><h3 class="nit-h3 nit-guarantee__subhead">The procedure</h3><ol class="nit-guarantee__steps" data-nit-stagger><li class="nit-guarantee__step nit-reveal" >
                    <span class="nit-guarantee__step-label nit-h3">Tell us</span>
                    <span class="nit-body nit-muted nit-guarantee__step-text">Email support with the order number and what it is doing. A person in the UK replies within one working day.</span>
                  </li><li class="nit-guarantee__step nit-reveal" >
                    <span class="nit-guarantee__step-label nit-h3">Send it back</span>
                    <span class="nit-body nit-muted nit-guarantee__step-text">We email a prepaid label. The postage is ours, not yours, and there is nothing to pay up front and reclaim later.</span>
                  </li><li class="nit-guarantee__step nit-reveal" >
                    <span class="nit-guarantee__step-label nit-h3">Replaced or refunded</span>
                    <span class="nit-body nit-muted nit-guarantee__step-text">Your choice rather than ours, settled within three working days of it reaching us. A replacement carries the remainder of the original term.</span>
                  </li></ol>
          </div><dl class="nit-guarantee__terms nit-nums nit-reveal"><div class="nit-guarantee__term" >
                  <dt class="nit-label nit-guarantee__term-key">Returns</dt>
                  <dd class="nit-guarantee__term-value">30 days, used or unused</dd>
                </div><div class="nit-guarantee__term" >
                  <dt class="nit-label nit-guarantee__term-key">Warranty</dt>
                  <dd class="nit-guarantee__term-value">2 years</dd>
                </div><div class="nit-guarantee__term" >
                  <dt class="nit-label nit-guarantee__term-key">Return postage</dt>
                  <dd class="nit-guarantee__term-value">We pay</dd>
                </div><div class="nit-guarantee__term" >
                  <dt class="nit-label nit-guarantee__term-key">Support</dt>
                  <dd class="nit-guarantee__term-value">UK, 1 working day</dd>
                </div></dl></div><div class="nit-guarantee__limits nit-reveal"><h3 class="nit-label nit-guarantee__limits-title">What this does not cover</h3><div class="nit-body nit-muted nit-measure nit-guarantee__limits-body">
            <p>Accidental damage is not covered &#8212; a dropped unit or a cracked housing is not a fault. The filter is a consumable: it washes rather than replaces, but it will not last the life of the vacuum and a new one is not a warranty claim. Battery capacity falls with use, and a cell holding less charge at the end of two years is wear rather than failure. Anything else that stops it working is ours to fix.</p>
          </div>
        </div></div>
  </div>
</section>

